WEBVTT

00:01:47.857 --> 00:01:50.860
I can't... run any more.

00:01:54.072 --> 00:01:54.781
Kabaji-<i>kun</i>!

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.034
Don't show any kindness.

00:01:58.034 --> 00:01:59.119
You'll be the one to get attacked.

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:04.457
Just think about saving yourself.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:18.471
"Evolution and Change"

00:02:19.264 --> 00:02:22.267
Gather round, everyone.

00:02:22.726 --> 00:02:25.854
The eagles are feeling good and
the weather's nice today...

00:02:25.854 --> 00:02:30.025
so we'll be having a sportsman hunt.

00:02:37.282 --> 00:02:39.451
What is this stupid hunt?

00:02:40.076 --> 00:02:43.038
That coach is crazy.

00:02:43.747 --> 00:02:46.499
I can't believe he'd cover
balloons in a scent

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.877
to attract eagles so they'll chase us.

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:51.796
If they pop our balloon, we're out.

00:02:52.047 --> 00:02:54.716
And washing a mountain
of loincloths awaits us.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.386
Listen up.

00:02:58.887 --> 00:03:04.517
Those who fail will wash every
last stain out of my loincloths.

00:03:08.772 --> 00:03:10.315
Anything but that.

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:13.651
We've gotta run, even if it kills us.

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:17.572
They found us! Run!

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:34.506
Hey.

00:03:34.506 --> 00:03:35.507
What?

00:03:35.507 --> 00:03:37.550
Why are you following me?

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:39.302
Why not?

00:03:39.302 --> 00:03:41.721
Don't you feel better
having someone with you?

00:03:42.305 --> 00:03:45.225
It's easier for them to
find me if you're with me.

00:03:47.977 --> 00:03:49.312
See? Like I said.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.691
I'll handle this.

00:04:01.449 --> 00:04:03.618
Don't get in my way.

00:04:03.618 --> 00:04:06.663
What? You're the one getting in <i>my </i>way.

00:04:06.663 --> 00:04:07.539
Huh?

00:04:07.539 --> 00:04:08.581
What?

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:20.427
They're coming!

00:04:20.969 --> 00:04:22.429
They're too fast!

00:04:34.232 --> 00:04:36.192
What a godsend.

00:04:36.192 --> 00:04:38.111
There's a mountain stream here.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.869
I've got an idea.

00:04:57.547 --> 00:04:59.215
It's just a bird.

00:04:59.215 --> 00:05:03.303
If we play dead, I'm sure
he'll leave us alone.

00:05:24.282 --> 00:05:25.950
Game and match, Shiraishi.

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:27.577
Six games to love.

00:05:29.287 --> 00:05:31.122
Game and match, Tachibana.

00:05:31.122 --> 00:05:32.665
Six games to love.

00:05:33.375 --> 00:05:35.752
The middle schoolers have been

00:05:35.752 --> 00:05:37.712
moving up practically every day.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.173
Aside from Oni-<i>san</i>,

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:43.009
Court 5 is filling up
with middle schoolers.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:47.430
Yeah, but there's a few guys who aren't

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:49.182
even showing half their potential.

00:05:49.683 --> 00:05:51.643
What do you think, Tokugawa?

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:55.188
You seem to be enjoying
yourself, Tanegashima-<i>san</i>.

00:05:56.564 --> 00:05:57.399
Is that so?

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:02.362
But as they keep moving up,
the difference in skill

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:05.115
between courts is tremendous.

00:06:05.573 --> 00:06:07.409
Look.

00:06:10.704 --> 00:06:11.871
They're too strong.

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:15.250
Court 3 beat all the Court 4 players.

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:19.254
This Court 3 and Court 4 team shuffle...

00:06:19.254 --> 00:06:21.589
I didn't think there'd be such
a difference in ability.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:23.925
Team shuffle?

00:06:23.925 --> 00:06:28.513
Couldn't we use that to rise
to the top more quickly?

00:06:29.055 --> 00:06:31.391
I'm not sure you're ready for it.

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:32.559
What?

00:06:32.892 --> 00:06:35.103
Come back after you've beaten Oni.

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:39.274
I doubt you'll be able
to do that, though.

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:43.778
See you later.

00:06:46.281 --> 00:06:47.907
Sounds interesting.

00:06:57.792 --> 00:06:59.252
Please, no!

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:01.588
Hey, stupid Richard Sakata!

00:07:01.588 --> 00:07:04.007
It's useless to just run in a straight line!

00:07:04.007 --> 00:07:06.134
Run in a zig-zag pattern once in a while!

00:07:06.593 --> 00:07:09.721
But I suck at zig-zagging!

00:07:15.977 --> 00:07:18.688
Hey, Mukahi. If you jump too
high, the eagles will go for you.

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:20.899
Evade them with a low Moonsault.

00:07:21.358 --> 00:07:23.109
A low Moonsault?

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:24.194
What is that?

00:07:24.486 --> 00:07:25.612
Just do it.

00:07:26.112 --> 00:07:27.697
If you don't, you're done for.

00:07:34.996 --> 00:07:36.122
This way.

00:07:36.873 --> 00:07:38.541
They'll get you if you stay out there.

00:07:39.417 --> 00:07:40.418
Damn it.

00:07:40.835 --> 00:07:43.463
How long are we supposed to keep running?

00:07:43.797 --> 00:07:45.131
We have no choice.

00:07:45.131 --> 00:07:47.884
This is the only thing we can do.

00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:51.054
This is super lame.

00:07:53.098 --> 00:07:56.226
I'm sick of running and hiding.

00:07:57.519 --> 00:07:58.520
Shishido-<i>kun</i>.

00:08:00.563 --> 00:08:02.148
Bring it on!

00:08:02.148 --> 00:08:05.527
I'll read your every move!

00:08:07.237 --> 00:08:09.447
Looks like we lost them.

00:08:10.699 --> 00:08:13.952
My legs are jelly.

00:08:13.952 --> 00:08:17.330
What's that coach thinking?

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:19.791
He is crazy,

00:08:19.791 --> 00:08:22.919
but I doubt he's doing this
just for his own entertainment.

00:08:23.795 --> 00:08:25.338
What do you mean?

00:08:25.338 --> 00:08:26.798
Take a look.

00:08:28.425 --> 00:08:32.929
Did we really run up such a steep slope?

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:37.267
I didn't even notice how rocky it was.

00:08:38.893 --> 00:08:39.978
Pupina.

00:08:47.068 --> 00:08:48.695
Hey, Black Hat.

00:08:49.362 --> 00:08:52.657
It's not like you to hide.

00:08:53.908 --> 00:08:58.079
I've still got to thank
you for what you did.

00:08:58.872 --> 00:09:00.123
No thanks.

00:09:00.123 --> 00:09:02.959
Don't be like that, friend.

00:09:03.877 --> 00:09:06.755
I owe you a lot!

00:09:06.755 --> 00:09:09.632
You're all going to hell!

00:09:11.718 --> 00:09:12.719
Huh?

00:09:12.719 --> 00:09:14.012
Where'd he go?

00:09:14.596 --> 00:09:16.973
As swift as the wind.

00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:20.977
You should be careful.

00:09:21.353 --> 00:09:23.855
If you let your guard down,
you'll find yourself under attack.

00:09:23.855 --> 00:09:25.315
Moron.

00:09:25.315 --> 00:09:29.027
I washed the scent off
my balloon in a stream.

00:09:29.986 --> 00:09:35.909
Hate to tell you, but the eagles
stopped targeting me long ago.

00:09:46.461 --> 00:09:47.629
What's going on?

00:09:47.962 --> 00:09:49.214
Fool.

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:51.966
Bingo.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:53.468
You guys!

00:09:54.594 --> 00:09:56.805
Hold on, Koshimae.

00:09:56.805 --> 00:10:00.475
The chestnut I returned is the one
that popped his balloon.

00:10:00.475 --> 00:10:01.893
What are you talking about?

00:10:01.893 --> 00:10:03.061
It was mine.

00:10:03.061 --> 00:10:05.605
No, mine.

00:10:05.605 --> 00:10:06.481
Mine!

00:10:06.481 --> 00:10:07.982
It's mine!

00:10:07.982 --> 00:10:09.109
Fine.

00:10:09.109 --> 00:10:11.778
Let's decide this with a duel.

00:10:12.278 --> 00:10:13.655
I'm fine with that.

00:10:13.655 --> 00:10:16.449
I've been wanting to settle things
once and for all, anyway.

00:10:28.211 --> 00:10:31.881
How about, if this falls on your
side of the court, you lose?

00:10:31.881 --> 00:10:34.217
Sounds good. This'll be fun.

00:10:34.926 --> 00:10:36.136
Here we go.

00:10:45.729 --> 00:10:46.938
What are they doing?

00:10:48.481 --> 00:10:49.858
Talk about confidence.

00:10:49.858 --> 00:10:52.402
This isn't enough.

00:10:52.402 --> 00:10:54.612
How about this?

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:58.158
Two can play at that game.

00:11:01.703 --> 00:11:02.954
Seriously?

00:11:02.954 --> 00:11:07.000
They're volleying three
chestnuts at the same time.

00:11:19.137 --> 00:11:22.724
No, no, no!

00:11:22.724 --> 00:11:23.725
Well, what do you know, Sakata?

00:11:24.267 --> 00:11:28.188
You've mastered zig-zagging.

00:11:28.438 --> 00:11:29.439
Mukahi, in front of you!

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:36.321
I still don't know what it is,
but I'll try this low Moonsault.

00:11:50.627 --> 00:11:53.463
I did it... I think.

00:11:53.922 --> 00:11:54.964
Mukahi!

00:12:04.432 --> 00:12:05.642
Amazing.

00:12:05.642 --> 00:12:09.521
He's moving in response
to the eagle's movements.

00:12:10.355 --> 00:12:13.108
More. Keep bringing it on.

00:12:14.275 --> 00:12:15.360
Bastard.

00:12:15.819 --> 00:12:18.405
Get ready, Koshimae.

00:12:19.948 --> 00:12:20.824
What?

00:12:23.993 --> 00:12:26.913
What are you doing, you idiot?!

00:12:50.729 --> 00:12:52.188
Look at that.

00:12:52.188 --> 00:12:53.565
E-Echizen?

00:12:58.945 --> 00:13:00.196
This isn't good.

00:13:00.196 --> 00:13:02.073
He's surrounded by eagles.

00:13:03.324 --> 00:13:06.327
Wh-What am I supposed to do?

00:13:07.078 --> 00:13:08.163
I know.

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:12.042
Koshimae!

00:13:12.584 --> 00:13:14.961
Take these!

00:13:31.102 --> 00:13:32.312
You can't be serious.

00:13:33.396 --> 00:13:37.067
They both hit five chestnuts
at the same time.

00:13:37.317 --> 00:13:39.736
D-Did you see that, Koshimae?

00:13:39.736 --> 00:13:44.157
I just hit five chestnuts at once!

00:13:47.494 --> 00:13:51.956
Looks like you're finally
moving a little better.

00:13:53.458 --> 00:13:54.626
It's the drunkard.

00:13:55.919 --> 00:13:59.297
But let me warn you.

00:14:00.423 --> 00:14:02.759
If you can't hit ten at the same time,

00:14:02.759 --> 00:14:05.095
you'll never beat Oni or Tokugawa.

00:14:06.638 --> 00:14:07.764
Really?

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:12.143
If I can hit ten at the same time,
I can beat them.

00:14:14.354 --> 00:14:16.815
Show me how to do it, then.

00:14:24.447 --> 00:14:26.908
Shut up, you brat!

00:14:28.785 --> 00:14:31.955
I hate naïve little brats
like you the most!

00:14:34.541 --> 00:14:36.710
What're you doing to Koshimae?

00:14:37.002 --> 00:14:39.045
Tell the rest of the trash,

00:14:39.587 --> 00:14:41.297
we're done for the day.

00:14:41.589 --> 00:14:42.882
You're dismissed.

00:15:00.316 --> 00:15:01.317
Ko--

00:15:02.068 --> 00:15:03.361
Koshimae...

00:15:13.705 --> 00:15:16.166
What? The sportsman hunt's over?

00:15:16.916 --> 00:15:17.876
We did it.

00:15:17.876 --> 00:15:19.544
We're saved.

00:15:20.045 --> 00:15:21.087
Why?

00:15:21.421 --> 00:15:25.717
Some middle schoolers chased
off all the eagles.

00:15:25.717 --> 00:15:26.551
What?

00:15:26.551 --> 00:15:29.512
I heard they've already started
practicing on their own.

00:15:29.512 --> 00:15:30.930
Seriously?

00:15:35.477 --> 00:15:37.562
I have a favor to ask you.

00:15:39.147 --> 00:15:41.483
My body feels unbelievably light.

00:15:47.822 --> 00:15:51.284
The irregular bounces
don't bother me at all.

00:15:52.243 --> 00:15:54.871
You mean by climbing through caves

00:15:54.871 --> 00:15:56.956
and running from eagles...

00:15:56.956 --> 00:15:58.792
we've strengthened our bodies

00:15:58.792 --> 00:16:01.753
and overcome our weaknesses?

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:04.464
I can't be certain,

00:16:04.464 --> 00:16:07.842
but on this uneven court no
one could play on at first...

00:16:08.343 --> 00:16:11.763
Everyone's rallying normally now.

00:16:13.431 --> 00:16:15.225
Now that you mention it,

00:16:15.225 --> 00:16:17.394
I feel like the caves and laser traps

00:16:17.394 --> 00:16:20.063
improved my poor balance.

00:16:20.438 --> 00:16:24.859
I mastered the low Moonsault
during the sportsman hunt.

00:16:25.694 --> 00:16:28.988
Is it possible... that Mifune guy...

00:16:35.203 --> 00:16:37.997
is actually an amazing coach?

00:16:50.927 --> 00:16:52.345
He's unbelievable.

00:16:53.513 --> 00:16:57.392
He didn't lose a single
point playing one on five.

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:21.875
Tomorrow's team shuffle is
between Courts 5 and 3.

00:17:22.417 --> 00:17:25.503
Oni's leading the middle schoolers

00:17:25.503 --> 00:17:28.715
from Court 5 against Irie-<i>san</i>'s Court 3?

00:17:28.715 --> 00:17:30.300
But, why?

00:17:32.802 --> 00:17:35.013
Tomorrow should be fun.

00:17:40.894 --> 00:17:43.813
"Locker Room (Court 5)"

00:17:44.022 --> 00:17:46.524
The team shuffle is a team match.

00:17:46.524 --> 00:17:48.651
We choose seven representatives

00:17:48.651 --> 00:17:52.072
to play three singles
and two doubles matches.

00:17:52.072 --> 00:17:54.616
If we win these five matches,

00:17:54.616 --> 00:17:57.577
we'll all swap courts with Court 3.

00:17:58.286 --> 00:18:00.789
I'll decide the lineup. Okay?

00:18:01.206 --> 00:18:02.499
Fine with me.

00:18:06.336 --> 00:18:09.339
But there's one thing that bothers me.

00:18:09.798 --> 00:18:13.009
As the gatekeeper,
you've defeated everyone

00:18:13.009 --> 00:18:15.345
who's risen to play you.

00:18:16.262 --> 00:18:18.765
Why are you doing this now?

00:18:22.644 --> 00:18:25.689
You've set fire to my heart.

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:28.066
That's all.

00:18:53.925 --> 00:18:55.802
This isn't like you.

00:18:57.012 --> 00:18:59.681
You've never been the emotional type.

00:18:59.681 --> 00:19:01.182
Mind your own business.

00:19:04.936 --> 00:19:06.104
Did you lose?

00:19:06.688 --> 00:19:09.024
I said mind your own business.

00:19:09.607 --> 00:19:10.775
Just listen.

00:19:11.276 --> 00:19:13.653
I lost to one of my former teammates.

00:19:15.196 --> 00:19:16.364
That's too bad.

00:19:16.364 --> 00:19:17.699
Just listen.

00:19:18.324 --> 00:19:22.162
We must get stronger and
rise up from this place.

00:19:22.162 --> 00:19:23.496
That's obvious.

00:19:23.496 --> 00:19:26.958
We can't afford to take it slow.

00:19:26.958 --> 00:19:28.209
Of course.

00:19:29.669 --> 00:19:32.964
That coach may be harsh,

00:19:32.964 --> 00:19:37.135
but he may be the fastest
route out of here.

00:19:37.677 --> 00:19:39.804
But he won't teach me.

00:19:40.722 --> 00:19:42.098
Then...

00:19:43.767 --> 00:19:47.228
Come. We'll get as much sake as we can.

00:19:49.064 --> 00:19:50.899
Hold it right there!

00:19:51.232 --> 00:19:55.278
We're not going to let you
guys run off on your own.

00:19:55.528 --> 00:19:59.783
I heard that bar lounge
is a real fun place.

00:19:59.783 --> 00:20:03.119
I was just thinking that I
wanted some more exercise.

00:20:03.119 --> 00:20:05.872
I'll perfect my low Moonsault.

00:20:06.289 --> 00:20:07.457
Guys...

00:20:07.832 --> 00:20:09.626
We'll go, too.

00:20:11.252 --> 00:20:14.506
I'll put my faith in your potential.

00:20:33.817 --> 00:20:37.237
He fell asleep.
Snoring like a chainsaw, at that.

00:20:38.071 --> 00:20:42.200
Looks like there wasn't any
point in getting all that sake.

00:20:51.167 --> 00:20:53.253
Six balls is my limit for now...

00:20:53.753 --> 00:20:58.508
But I'll definitely learn to hit ten at once.

00:21:01.469 --> 00:21:04.556
Can you keep up with my training?

00:21:05.306 --> 00:21:06.474
Of course.

00:21:17.235 --> 00:21:25.035
I've never liked those
arrogant U-17 coaches.

00:21:26.745 --> 00:21:29.372
Men, you must crush them!

00:21:29.956 --> 00:21:32.292
This is a revolution!

00:21:35.211 --> 00:21:40.842
All right! We'll show 'em! Let's do it!

00:23:17.063 --> 00:23:18.023
"Preview"

00:23:18.023 --> 00:23:18.982
"Preview"
Tezuka-<i>kun</i>.

00:23:18.982 --> 00:23:20.608
"Preview"
Captain Yamata, it's
good to see you again.

00:23:20.608 --> 00:23:21.276
Captain Yamata, it's
good to see you again.

00:23:21.276 --> 00:23:23.653
What are you doing here?

00:23:23.653 --> 00:23:24.237
What?

00:23:24.237 --> 00:23:26.656
Whose team invited you here?

00:23:26.656 --> 00:23:29.159
As a U-17 candidate,
I will do my best.

00:23:29.409 --> 00:23:31.369
That's the only thing
on my mind right now.

00:23:31.369 --> 00:23:37.417
Again? You've always sacrificed
yourself for the team.

00:23:37.417 --> 00:23:40.712
Isn't it about time you
set yourself free?

00:23:43.381 --> 00:23:45.258
"Farewell, Kunimitsu Tezuka"
The next episode of <i>Prince of Tennis II</i>
is: "Farewell, Kunimitsu Tezuka."

00:23:45.258 --> 00:23:47.136
"Farewell, Kunimitsu Tezuka"
Free...
